343	/// The props one merge has made, by what they were made from ([`MergeKey`]). A merged prop is a function of those
344	/// inputs and the merge's [`ResolverFacts`] alone, so a prop made from the same ones is the one made before: it skips
345	/// the copy, the reordering and the interning of a type that is often hundreds of members wide. Each entry holds the
346	/// two props its key points at, so neither is freed and its address taken by another prop while the merge runs.
347	#[derive(Default)]
348	struct MergeMemo {
349	    made: FxHashMap<MergeKey, MemoEntry>,
350	}
